  1044  p9  paragraph  [p9-l47]  B More Details of Pre-training Corpora
  1045  p9  paragraph  [p9-l48]  We use MAPS, the mobile application privacy pol-
  1046  p9  paragraph  [p9-l49]  icy corpus presented by Zimmeck et al. (2019).
  1047  p9  paragraph  [p9-l50]  MAPS consists of the URLs of 441K mobile ap-
  1048  p9  paragraph  [p9-l51]  plication privacy policies, which were collected
  1049  p9  paragraph  [p9-l52]  from April to May 2018 from the Google Play
  1050  p9  paragraph  [p9-l53]  store. We remove the duplicated URLs, crawl the
  1051  p9  paragraph  [p9-l54]  privacy policy documents in HTML/PDF format,
  1052  p9  paragraph  [p9-l55]  convert them to raw text format, and filter out the
  1053  p9  paragraph  [p9-l56]  documents with noise (e.g., empty documents re-
  1054  p9  paragraph  [p9-l57]  sulting from obsolete URLs). Finally, we ended
  1055  p9  paragraph  [p9-l58]  up with 64K privacy policy documents. For web-
  1056  p9  paragraph  [p9-l59]  site privacy policies, we use the Princeton-Leuven
  1057  p9  paragraph  [p9-l60]  Longitudinal Corpus of Privacy Policies (Amos
  1058  p9  paragraph  [p9-l61]  et al., 2021).4 The Princeton-Leuven Longitudinal
  1059  p9  paragraph  [p9-l62]  Corpus of Privacy Policies contains 130K website
  1060  p9  paragraph  [p9-l63]  privacy policies spanning over two decades. We
  1061  p9  paragraph  [p9-l64]  use the documents with the latest date and con-
  1062  p9  paragraph  [p9-l65]  vert them (from markdown format) into text format.
  1063  p9  paragraph  [p9-l66]  Combining these two corpora, we obtain our pre-
  1064  p9  paragraph  [p9-l67]  training corpus with 332M words.
  1065  p9  paragraph  [p9-l68]  C Baseline Models
  1066  p9  paragraph  [p9-l69]  We benchmark a few pre-trained language models
  1067  p9  paragraph  [p9-l70]  as baselines to facilitate future work.
  1068  p9  paragraph  [p9-l71]  BERT
  1069  p9  paragraph  [p9-l72]  Devlin et al. (2019) proposed Transformer
  1070  p9  paragraph  [p9-l73]  (Vaswani et al., 2017) based language model pre-
  1071  p9  paragraph  [p9-l74]  trained on BooksCorpus and English Wikipedia
  1072  p9  paragraph  [p9-l75]  data using masked language modeling (MLM) and
  1073  p9  paragraph  [p9-l76]  next sentence prediction.
  1074  p9  paragraph  [p9-l77]  Electra
  1075  p9  paragraph  [p9-l78]  Clark et al. (2020) pre-trains a generator
  1076  p9  paragraph  [p9-l79]  and a discriminator on the same corpus as BERT,
  1077  p9  paragraph  [p9-l80]  where the generator takes a masked text as input
  1078  p9  paragraph  [p9-l81]  and is trained using the MLM objective. The dis-
  1079  p9  paragraph  [p9-l82]  criminator takes the predictions from the generator
  1080  p9  paragraph  [p9-l83]  and detects which tokens are replaced by the gener-
  1081  p9  paragraph  [p9-l84]  ator. After pre-training, the generator is discarded,
  1082  p9  paragraph  [p9-l85]  and the discriminator is used as the language model
  1083  p9  paragraph  [p9-l86]  for the downstream tasks.
  1084  p9  paragraph  [p9-l87]  SpanBERT
  1085  p9  paragraph  [p9-l88]  Joshi et al. (2020) shares the same
  1086  p9  paragraph  [p9-l89]  architecture and pre-training corpus as BERT but
  1087  p9  paragraph  [p9-l90]  differs in the pre-training objectives. It extends
  1088  p9  paragraph  [p9-l91]  BERT by masking contiguous spans instead of sin-
  1089  p9  paragraph  [p9-l92]  gle tokens and training the span boundary represen-
  1090  p9  paragraph  [p9-l93]  tations to predict the masked spans.
  1091  p9  paragraph  [p9-l94]  RoBERTa
  1092  p9  paragraph  [p9-l95]  Liu et al. (2019) presented a replica-
  1093  p9  paragraph  [p9-l96]  tion study of BERT pretraining where they showed
  1094  p9  paragraph  [p9-l97]  that BERT was significantly undertrained and pro-
  1095  p9  paragraph  [p9-l98]  posed RoBERTa that tunes key hyperparameters
  1096  p9  figure  [p9-d1]  
  1097  p9  paragraph  [p9-l99]  4The corpus is publicly available at https://github.
  1098  p9  paragraph  [p9-l100]  com/citp/privacy-policy-historical.
