  342  p4  paragraph  [p4-l13]  6 Analysis
  343  p4  paragraph  [p4-l14]  For the two most powerful models, it is clear that
  344  p4  paragraph  [p4-l15]  ellipsis poses a difficult challenge, except in the two
  345  p4  paragraph  [p4-l16]  simplest ellipsis structures. For the less powerful
  346  p4  paragraph  [p4-l17]  models, the picture is mixed. For these models,
  347  p4  paragraph  [p4-l18]  the non-ellipsis examples are themselves a difficult
  348  p4  paragraph  [p4-l19]  challenge, so we are not able to observe the specific
  349  p4  paragraph  [p4-l20]  difficulties posed by ellipsis.
  350  p4  paragraph  [p4-l21]  As we can see in figure 1, the Davinci-002 model
  351  p4  paragraph  [p4-l22]  performs somewhat better overall than Davinci-
  352  p4  figure  [p4-i3]  
  353  p4  paragraph  [p4-l23]  Figure 3: Ellipsis Accuracy – davinci-002 (1000 exam-
  354  p4  paragraph  [p4-l24]  ples per structure.)
  355  p4  figure  [p4-i4]  
  356  p4  paragraph  [p4-l25]  Figure 4: Ellipsis Accuracy – curie-001 (1000 examples
  357  p4  paragraph  [p4-l26]  per structure.)
  358  p4  paragraph  [p4-l27]  003, on both ellipsis and non-ellipsis. However,
  359  p4  paragraph  [p4-l28]  figures 2 and 3 show that the advantage of Davinci-
  360  p4  paragraph  [p4-l29]  002 on ellipsis is exclusively due to the subordi-
  361  p4  paragraph  [p4-l30]  nate antecedent construction. In every other el-
  362  p4  paragraph  [p4-l31]  lipsis structure, Davinci-003 performs better than
  363  p4  paragraph  [p4-l32]  Davinci-002.
  364  p4  paragraph  [p4-l33]  There are striking differences in the distribution
  365  p4  paragraph  [p4-l34]  of errors. For both the Davinci-003 and Davinci-
  366  p4  paragraph  [p4-l35]  002 models, errors are nearly always false negatives
  367  p4  paragraph  [p4-l36]  – that is, incorrect “No" answers. There are virtually
  368  p4  paragraph  [p4-l37]  no false positives, either for the ellipsis case or non-
  369  p4  paragraph  [p4-l38]  ellipsis case. For the other three models, there are
  370  p4  paragraph  [p4-l39]  many errors of each type, with a much higher ratio
  371  p4  paragraph  [p4-l40]  of false positives.
  372  p4  paragraph  [p4-l41]  7 Conclusion
  373  p4  paragraph  [p4-l42]  Most of the current rapid progress in NLP is due
  374  p4  paragraph  [p4-l43]  to pre-trained large language models. GPT-3 is
  375  p4  paragraph  [p4-l44]  an impressive publicly available collection of such
  376  p4  furniture  [p4-l45]  42
  377  p5  figure  [p5-i1]  
  378  p5  paragraph  [p5-l1]  Figure 5: Ellipsis Accuracy – babbage-001 (1000 exam-
  379  p5  paragraph  [p5-l2]  ples per structure.)
  380  p5  figure  [p5-i2]  
  381  p5  paragraph  [p5-l3]  Figure 6: Ellipsis Accuracy – ada-001 (1000 examples
  382  p5  paragraph  [p5-l4]  per structure.)
  383  p5  paragraph  [p5-l5]  models, and is able to perform in a way that sug-
  384  p5  paragraph  [p5-l6]  gests human-level understanding. Because of this,
  385  p5  paragraph  [p5-l7]  it is important to explore areas in which it might
  386  p5  paragraph  [p5-l8]  still differ from human language understanding. In
  387  p5  paragraph  [p5-l9]  this paper we have argued that ellipsis is one such
  388  p5  paragraph  [p5-l10]  area. For many simple ellipsis structures, the most
  389  p5  paragraph  [p5-l11]  powerful GPT-3 models struggle, with accuracies
  390  p5  paragraph  [p5-l12]  far lower on ellipsis examples than on non-elliptical
  391  p5  paragraph  [p5-l13]  counterparts.
  392  p5  paragraph  [p5-l14]  In many ways, GPT-3 appears to understand
  393  p5  paragraph  [p5-l15]  the texts that it processes, often being able to
  394  p5  paragraph  [p5-l16]  answer questions that appear to rely on sophisti-
  395  p5  paragraph  [p5-l17]  cated reasoning. However, the challenge of ellipsis-
  396  p5  paragraph  [p5-l18]  dependent reasoning provides evidence that GPT-3
  397  p5  paragraph  [p5-l19]  is not able to understand in anything like the way
  398  p5  paragraph  [p5-l20]  humans do.
  399  p5  figure  [p5-i3]  
