  404  p5  paragraph  [p5-l24]  Figure 8: Non-ellipsis case – Errors by model. False
  405  p5  paragraph  [p5-l25]  Positives (Incorrect “Yes") vs. False Negatives (Incor-
  406  p5  paragraph  [p5-l26]  rect “No")
  407  p5  paragraph  [p5-l27]  8 Limitations
  408  p5  paragraph  [p5-l28]  This paper argues that the proposed task of ellipsis-
  409  p5  paragraph  [p5-l29]  dependent reasoning is a difficult challenge for
  410  p5  paragraph  [p5-l30]  GPT-3 models, which are among the most power-
  411  p5  paragraph  [p5-l31]  ful current language models. The data constructed
  412  p5  paragraph  [p5-l32]  here is restricted to English, and furthermore is re-
  413  p5  paragraph  [p5-l33]  stricted to a single form of ellipsis, namely verb
  414  p5  paragraph  [p5-l34]  phrase ellipsis. It may well be that other forms of
  415  p5  paragraph  [p5-l35]  ellipsis may give rise to different effects, and it is
  416  p5  paragraph  [p5-l36]  also important to test the claims made here on other
  417  p5  paragraph  [p5-l37]  languages.
