  1034  p11  paragraph  [p11-l15]  6:
  1035  p11  paragraph  [p11-l16]  for k ∈ 0, . . . , N :
  1036  p11  paragraph  [p11-l17]  7:
  1037  p11  paragraph  [p11-l18]  for X ∈ N :
  1038  p11  paragraph  [p11-l19]  ▷ Prefix weight of ε
  1039  p11  paragraph  [p11-l20]  8:
  1040  p11  paragraph  [p11-l21]  π(k, X, k) ←− treesum(X)
  1041  p11  paragraph  [p11-l22]  9:
  1042  p11  paragraph  [p11-l23]  β ←− CKY(w)
  1043  p11  paragraph  [p11-l24]  ▷ Compute β with Alg. 1
  1044  p11  paragraph  [p11-l25]  10:
  1045  p11  paragraph  [p11-l26]  for i, j = 0, . . . , N :
  1046  p11  paragraph  [p11-l27]  11:
  1047  p11  paragraph  [p11-l28]  for X, Z ∈ N :
  1048  p11  paragraph  [p11-l29]  ▷ Compute γ by Eq. (16e)
  1049  p11  paragraph  [p11-l30]  12:
  1050  p11  paragraph  [p11-l31]  γij (X, Z)←− L
  1051  p11  paragraph  [p11-l33]  p(X−→YZ) ⊗ β(i, Y, j)
  1052  p11  paragraph  [p11-l32]  Y∈N
  1053  p11  paragraph  [p11-l34]  13:
  1054  p11  paragraph  [p11-l35]  for X, Z ∈ N :
  1055  p11  paragraph  [p11-l36]  ▷ Compute δ by Eq. (16f)
  1056  p11  paragraph  [p11-l37]  14:
  1057  p11  paragraph  [p11-l38]  δij (X, Z)←− L
  1058  p11  paragraph  [p11-l40]  ξ(Y | X) ⊗ γij (Y, Z)
  1059  p11  paragraph  [p11-l39]  Y∈N
  1060  p11  paragraph  [p11-l41]  15:
  1061  p11  paragraph  [p11-l42]  for k ∈ 0, . . . , N − 1 :
  1062  p11  paragraph  [p11-l43]  16:
  1063  p11  paragraph  [p11-l44]  for X ∈ N :
  1064  p11  paragraph  [p11-l45]  ▷ Compute base case
  1065  p11  paragraph  [p11-l46]  17:
  1066  p11  paragraph  [p11-l47]  π(k, X, k+1)←− L
  1067  p11  paragraph  [p11-l49]  ξ(Y | X) ⊗ p(Y−→wk+1)
  1068  p11  paragraph  [p11-l48]  Y∈N
  1069  p11  paragraph  [p11-l50]  18:
  1070  p11  paragraph  [p11-l51]  for ℓ ∈ 2 . . . N :
  1071  p11  paragraph  [p11-l52]  19:
  1072  p11  paragraph  [p11-l53]  for i ∈ 1 . . . N − ℓ :
  1073  p11  paragraph  [p11-l54]  20:
  1074  p11  paragraph  [p11-l55]  k ←− i + ℓ
  1075  p11  paragraph  [p11-l56]  21:
  1076  p11  paragraph  [p11-l57]  for X, Z ∈ N :
  1077  p11  paragraph  [p11-l58]  ▷ Recursively compute π
  1078  p11  paragraph  [p11-l61]  k
  1079  p11  paragraph  [p11-l63]  −1
  1080  p11  paragraph  [p11-l59]  22:
  1081  p11  paragraph  [p11-l60]  π(i, X, k) +=
  1082  p11  paragraph  [p11-l62]  L
  1083  p11  paragraph  [p11-l65]  δij (X, Z) ⊗ π(j, Z, k)
  1084  p11  paragraph  [p11-l64]  j=i+1
  1085  p11  paragraph  [p11-l66]  23:
  1086  p11  paragraph  [p11-l67]  return π
  1087  p11  figure  [p11-d3]  
  1088  p11  paragraph  [p11-l68]  Proposition 4. The semiring-weighted version of our algorithm runs in O(N2 |N |3 + N3 |N |2 ).
  1089  p11  paragraph  [p11-l69]  Proof. Lehmann’s algorithm, as presented in Alg. 4, has three nested for loops of d iterations each, where
  1090  p11  paragraph  [p11-l70]  d is the dimension of the input matrix. In our case, d is the number of non-terminals, |N |. Assuming the
  1091  p11  paragraph  [p11-l71]  Kleene closure of elements in W can be evaluated in O(1), this means that computing the left corner
  1092  p11  paragraph  [p11-l72]  expectations in line 1 of Alg. 5 takes O(|N |3 ), as before. Hence, the complexity of the overall algorithm
  1093  p11  paragraph  [p11-l73]  remains unchanged, that is, we can compute the prefix probabilities under a semiring-weighted, locally
  1094  p11  paragraph  [p11-l74]  normalized CFG G in O(N2 |N |3 + N3 |N |2 ).
  1095  p11  paragraph  [p11-l75]  ■
