  162  p2  paragraph  [p2-l53]  the dominance of extrinsic mechanisms reveals the strong
  163  p2  paragraph  [p2-l54]  role played by disorder-induced interband coherence in
  164  p2  paragraph  [p2-l55]  the transport of OAM. The OAM is an interband effect,
  165  p2  paragraph  [p2-l56]  and its intrinsic part is large in systems exhibiting large
  166  p2  paragraph  [p2-l57]  Berry curvatures, in other words, strong intrinsic inter-
  167  p2  paragraph  [p2-l58]  band coherence. On the other hand, skew scattering and
  168  p2  paragraph  [p2-l59]  side jump are sources of interband coherence mediated by
  169  p2  paragraph  [p2-l60]  disorder. Our calculation shows that, in the case of the
  170  p2  paragraph  [p2-l61]  OHE, this disorder-mediated contribution is one order of
  171  p2  paragraph  [p2-l62]  magnitude larger than the intrinsic terms, suggesting the
  172  p2  paragraph  [p2-l63]  best method to maximize the orbital Hall current may be
  173  p2  paragraph  [p2-l64]  to harness extrinsic mechanisms. Importantly, to obtain
  174  p2  paragraph  [p2-l65]  a large OHE it is not necessary for the Berry curvature
  175  p2  paragraph  [p2-l66]  to be large, a finding that has profound implications for
  176  p2  paragraph  [p2-l67]  the electrical manipulation of magnetic moments.
  177  p2  paragraph  [p2-l68]  Kinetic equation. We start with the quantum Liouville
  178  p2  paragraph  [p2-l69]  equation for the single-particle density operator ˆρ,
