  250  p2  paragraph  [p2-l130]  The disorder averaged density matrix ⟨ρˆ⟩ = ρ0 + ρE
  251  p2  paragraph  [p2-l131]  with ρ0 the density matrix in equilibrium and correction
  252  p2  paragraph  [p2-l132]  by external electrical field ρE = nE + SE. The kinetic
  253  p2  paragraph  [p2-l133]  equation is solved in terms of band-diagonal contribution
  254  p2  paragraph  [p2-l134]  nE and band off-diagonal contribution SE. The expec-
  255  p2  paragraph  [p2-l135]  tation value of the orbital Hall current is calculated as
  256  p2  paragraph  [p2-l136]  j = Tr[⟨ρˆ⟩ ˆj] and Tr represents the full operator trace,
  257  p2  paragraph  [p2-l137]  and we focus on ˆj z y = 1/2{Lˆ z, vˆy}. Transport theory
  258  p2  paragraph  [p2-l138]  requires EF τ /ℏ ≫ 1, where τ represents a character-
  259  p2  paragraph  [p2-l139]  istic momentum relaxation time that can be used as a
  260  p2  paragraph  [p2-l140]  measure of the disorder strength. The theory is formu-
  261  p2  paragraph  [p2-l141]  lated as an expansion in the small parameter ℏ/(EF τ ).
