  326  p3  paragraph  [p3-l35]  The skew scattering and side jump contributions
  327  p3  paragraph  [p3-l36]  to OH-conductance σOH vs the Fermi energy EF : (a) for the
  328  p3  paragraph  [p3-l37]  2H-phase monolayer MoS2 with the parameters vF = 3.6eV˚A
  329  p3  paragraph  [p3-l38]  and ∆ = 0.883eV; (b) for the tilted 2D massive Dirac model
  330  p3  paragraph  [p3-l39]  with vF = 1eV˚A and ∆ = 0.1eV and vt = 0.1vF .
  331  p3  paragraph  [p3-l40]  S (0)
  332  p3  paragraph  [p3-l41]  E into J 1st
  333  p3  paragraph  [p3-l42]  dia [S (0)
  334  p3  paragraph  [p3-l43]  E ] to get the zero-order n (0)
  335  p3  paragraph  [p3-l44]  E . This contri-
  336  p3  paragraph  [p3-l45]  bution is contained in vertex corrections in the diagram-
  337  p3  paragraph  [p3-l46]  matic formalism [53, 58]. These corrections represent
  338  p3  paragraph  [p3-l47]  spin/pseudospin-dependent scattering commonly termed
  339  p3  paragraph  [p3-l48]  skew scattering and side jump. They are associated with
  340  p3  paragraph  [p3-l49]  the Fermi surface, and occur because the scattering po-
  341  p3  paragraph  [p3-l50]  tential also contributes to band mixing and inter-band
  342  p3  paragraph  [p3-l51]  coherence. In this connection, an alternative interpre-
  343  p3  paragraph  [p3-l52]  tation is that disorder mixes the bands in the crystal,
  344  p3  paragraph  [p3-l53]  giving a correction to the wave function, and this results
  345  p3  paragraph  [p3-l54]  in a correction to the band-expectation values of certain
  346  p3  paragraph  [p3-l55]  physical observables, which is proportional to the disor-
  347  p3  paragraph  [p3-l56]  der strength. At the same time, an electric field shifts the
  348  p3  paragraph  [p3-l57]  Fermi surface away from equilibrium, and this shift is in-
  349  p3  paragraph  [p3-l58]  versely proportional to the disorder strength. The net
  350  p3  paragraph  [p3-l59]  result in the average of physical observables is the prod-
  351  p3  paragraph  [p3-l60]  uct of the correction to the band-expectation value and
  352  p3  paragraph  [p3-l61]  the shift in the distribution function, and this product is
  353  p3  paragraph  [p3-l62]  formally independent of the disorder strength.
  354  p3  paragraph  [p3-l63]  The intrinsic OHE arises from the intrinsic driving
  355  p3  paragraph  [p3-l64]  term Dmm′
