  719  p5  paragraph  [p5-l126]  (2021).
  720  p5  paragraph  [p5-l127]  [56] Z. Z. Du, C. M. Wang, H.-P. Sun, H.-Z. Lu, and X. C.
  721  p5  paragraph  [p5-l128]  Xie, Nature Communications 12, 5038 (2021).
  722  p5  paragraph  [p5-l129]  [57] Z. Z. Du, H.-Z. Lu,
  723  p5  paragraph  [p5-l130]  and X. C. Xie, Nature Reviews
  724  p5  paragraph  [p5-l131]  Physics 3, 744 (2021).
  725  p5  paragraph  [p5-l132]  [58] R. B. Atencia, Q. Niu, and D. Culcer, Phys. Rev. Res.
  726  p5  paragraph  [p5-l133]  4, 013001 (2022).
  727  p5  paragraph  [p5-l134]  [59] The limit of ∆ → 0 is related to the fact that the integral
  728  p5  paragraph  [p5-l135]  of a limit and the limit of an integral are generally not
  729  p6  furniture  [p6-l1]  6
  730  p6  paragraph  [p6-l2]  the same. This behaviour is also present in the Berry
  731  p6  paragraph  [p6-l3]  curvature, as discussed in Ref. [81] for anomalous Hall
  732  p6  paragraph  [p6-l4]  effect. In this paper, if we take the ∆ → 0 at the very
  733  p6  paragraph  [p6-l5]  beginning of graphene Hamiltonian, the OHE disappears
  734  p6  paragraph  [p6-l6]  altogether. But if we take the ∆ → 0 limit for the orbital
  735  p6  paragraph  [p6-l7]  moment, it yields lim∆→0∆/(q 2 v 2 F + ∆2 ) = πδ(q 2 v 2 F ).
  736  p6  paragraph  [p6-l8]  For the intrinsic case, the Fermi energy lies exactly at the
  737  p6  paragraph  [p6-l9]  Dirac point. The ∆ → 0 limit will make the intrinsic OH-
  738  p6  paragraph  [p6-l10]  conductance diverge after performing the integral over
  739  p6  paragraph  [p6-l11]  the Fermi sea [33]. Hence, formally, the intrinsic OH-
  740  p6  paragraph  [p6-l12]  conductance will diverge when the EF is in band gap and
  741  p6  paragraph  [p6-l13]  the extrinsic OH-conductance will vanish for graphene.
  742  p6  paragraph  [p6-l14]  However, in realistic samples, we expect that once the
  743  p6  paragraph  [p6-l15]  gap reaches below a certain value it will be overwhelmed
  744  p6  paragraph  [p6-l16]  by disorder and such a divergence will not be observable
  745  p6  paragraph  [p6-l17]  in practice. The limit of vanishing gap makes sense only
  746  p6  paragraph  [p6-l18]  for graphene which is a gapless material in a pristine
  747  p6  paragraph  [p6-l19]  situation. The ∆ → 0 limit is not applicable to TMDs,
  748  p6  paragraph  [p6-l20]  since the band gap of monolayer TMDs is inherent to the
  749  p6  paragraph  [p6-l21]  band structure of materials [45].
  750  p6  paragraph  [p6-l22]  [60] T. Tanaka, H. Kontani, M. Naito, T. Naito, D. S. Hi-
